# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. Dev machines here are Windows with
# core.autocrlf on, which would check these out with CRLF — and a CRLF shebang
# fails as `/usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory`, both in
# Git Bash and anywhere the script runs in a container. The failure looks like a
# missing interpreter, not a line-ending problem, so it costs real time.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for container/entrypoint files that shells parse.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
